# Line endings, stated rather than left to each contributor's git config.
#
# Without this file git translates text to CRLF on a Windows checkout, and the
# golden corpus in cmd/graphene/testdata/golden is compared byte for byte
# against output the CLI writes with LF. Every case in TestGoldenOutput then
# fails on windows-latest with a diff that looks identical when printed, which
# is the worst kind of red: correct code, unreadable failure.
#
# text=auto still detects binary content and leaves it alone, so fixtures and
# fuzz corpora are unaffected.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF wherever they run: a CRLF shebang line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named "sh\r".
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is content either way; pinned so the two runners match.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
